  <h1>Safety & Scam Awareness Guide</h1>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 1.5rem">1. General Safety Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Always verify the identity of anyone you plan to room with or share transportation with.</li>
    <li>Use video calls (Zoom, Teams, FaceTime) before committing to sharing accommodations.</li>
    <li>Ask for institutional affiliation (e.g., university, research group) and verify it independently.</li>
    <li>Meet in a public place (such as the conference venue) before traveling together or exchanging keys.</li>
    <li>Trust your instincts — if a conversation feels off, disengage.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 1.5rem">2. Protecting Your Personal Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Do not share your home address, passport details, or financial information with other users.</li>
    <li>Use your professional or institutional email rather than a personal one if possible.</li>
    <li>Avoid sending photos of IDs or travel documents.</li>
    <li>Do not make payments or reimbursements until you have confirmed details with the other person.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 1.5rem">3. Recognizing Scam Behavior</h2>
  <p>Be cautious if someone:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Avoids video calls or claims their camera is "broken."</li>
    <li>Pressures you to commit quickly or demands payment up front.</li>
    <li>Sends unusually low-cost offers that seem too good to be true.</li>
    <li>Asks for gift cards, cryptocurrency, wire transfers, or unusual payment methods.</li>
    <li>Claims an "emergency" that requires immediate money.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If any of these occur, do not proceed.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 1.5rem">4. Money & Payment Safety</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Whenever possible, make hotel or car reservations through official websites where costs can be split at check-in.</li>
    <li>If sharing costs (such as an Airbnb), make sure all names are on the reservation when possible.</li>
    <li>Use secure and traceable payment methods (Venmo, PayPal, or bank transfer), not cash or gift cards.</li>
    <li>Keep screenshots or receipts of all agreements.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 1.5rem">5. Meeting & Rooming Safety</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Choose hotels that have 24/7 staff and security.</li>
    <li>Share your travel plans with a colleague or friend.</li>
    <li>When you first meet your roommate, do so in a public, well-lit area.</li>
    <li>Lock valuables in your luggage or use hotel safes.</li>
    <li>Set clear expectations ahead of time (e.g., sleeping schedule, visitors, noise, shared rides).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 1.5rem">6. Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>Research Roomies does not verify user identities and cannot guarantee user reliability. Users are responsible for conducting their own due diligence and for their own personal safety.</p>
